# Shared CSS Styles (Web)

Do **not** create new TypeScript files that export shared Tailwind/class strings (e.g. `export const BUTTON_CLASS = "..."`) for cross-file reuse.

## When Styles Are Reused

If the same class list appears in **two or more** places, add a utility class in `src/apps/web/src/assets/styles/base.css` (same pattern as `.btn-primary`, `.form-input`) and use `className="utility-name"` in components.

```css
/* base.css */
.popover-menu-item {
  @apply block w-full px-3 py-2 text-left text-sm ...;
}
```

```tsx
<button type="button" className="popover-menu-item">Edit</button>
```

## When Inline Classes Are Fine

- One-off layout or page-specific styling
- Component-local styling not reused elsewhere
- Dynamic class composition (`granted ? "..." : "..."`) inside a single component

## Do Not (New Code)

- Export `const MENU_ITEM_CLASS = "..."` from a `.ts` file for cross-file reuse
- Re-export style constants from route `helpers.ts` for JSX `className` usage

Existing constants (for example overlay z-index in `src/apps/web/src/utils/constant.ts`) may remain until Phase 8 consolidation; do not add more.

## Where to Add Shared Classes

`src/apps/web/src/assets/styles/base.css` — use `@apply` with Tailwind utilities; keep names short and semantic (`account-tile-grid`, not `creditCardAccountTileGridClass`).
